@startuml
title MVP content safety versus future executable code
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
rectangle "MVP supplied content\nUploads / rich text / repository files" as U
rectangle "Current authority + supported type/size/quota\nSafe validation and rendering" as V
rectangle "Private same-server library / selected display\nAuthorized direct and byte-range access" as C
U --> V
V --> C
rectangle "AFTER MVP: executable repository/YAML workloads" as X #4A302B
rectangle "Future isolation / secrets / network / resource proof\nSeparate exact target approval" as T #4A302B
X --> T
note bottom of C
 Accepting data never authorizes execution.
 No heavyweight transcoding or in-product editor required by MVP.
end note
@enduml
